Hi!

I'm plotting an unrooted tree with the following command
p <- ggtree(tree,layout="unrooted") +
  geom_tippoint(size=2)
but, as you can see, the  terminal branches of the tree overlap extensively, which makes difficult to identify how many individuals belong to each clade.

 <https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-YFmpNSk9Xb8/WG5WrsvRItI/AAAAAAAAAHs/WDXCvrQddcYSDtxoGQUTcprLgX9nJZafACLcB/s1600/ggtree.png>
A rendition of the same tree with standard plot produces a better results:
plot(tree,type="unrooted",show.tip.label=FALSE)

 <https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-XD0w5My170g/WG5XRZqFSqI/AAAAAAAAAHw/pCHc7dmQfcYVhYL1sGPDM4SFTmySzrQuQCLcB/s1600/ape765.png>

 It would be perfect if I could emulate this branch distribution. So, how can I tell ggtree to produce more even spaces between branches?

