I would like to plot a tree with the 95% HPD's of the node height displayed. From the vignette I see this can be easily done with the following code:
plot(beast, annotation="length_0.95_HPD", branch.length="none") + theme_tree()

However, when performing my beast analysis I left the evolutionary rate set to 1 and thus must scale my tree accordingly. Is there an easy way to do this? I have tried a couple things with no success. I would rather avoid the mess of converting the beast class to a dataframe and parsing and manipulating the data if there is an easy way to manipulate the fields.

plot(beast, annotation="length_0.95_HPD"*316743.4, branch.length="none") + theme_tree()

#I've previously been able to scale the tree branches with the following
tre.g@phylo$edge.length <- tre.g@phylo$edge.length * 316743.4

#But when I try to access the length_0.95_HPD field I have trouble
tree@fields[14] <- tree@fields[14]*316743.4

